{% extends "layouts/docs" %}

{% block content %}
	<p>Install Kiln from npm:</p>

	{% apply highlight("sh") %}
		{% verbatim %}
npm install @lucidkiln/core
		{% endverbatim %}
	{% endapply %}

	<p>Kiln needs Node 24 or 26, or Cloudflare Workers. It is an ES module and includes its own TypeScript types. Template files use the <code>.kiln</code> extension.</p>

	<h2>Node</h2>

	<p>On Node, use <code>fileLoader</code> to read templates from a folder. It comes from a separate entry point, <code>@lucidkiln/core/node</code>, so it never ends up in a Workers bundle.</p>

	{% apply highlight("ts") %}
		{% verbatim %}
import { createKiln } from "@lucidkiln/core";
import { fileLoader } from "@lucidkiln/core/node";

const kiln = createKiln({
	loader: fileLoader({ root: "templates" }),
});
		{% endverbatim %}
	{% endapply %}

	<h2>Cloudflare Workers</h2>

	<p>Workers can't read files, so pass the templates in as strings with <code>memoryLoader</code>. How you collect them depends on your build. Most bundlers can import a file as text.</p>

	{% apply highlight("ts") %}
		{% verbatim %}
import { createKiln, memoryLoader } from "@lucidkiln/core";
import layout from "./templates/layouts/base.kiln?raw";
import home from "./templates/pages/home.kiln?raw";

const kiln = createKiln({
	loader: memoryLoader({
		"layouts/base.kiln": layout,
		"pages/home.kiln": home,
	}),
});
		{% endverbatim %}
	{% endapply %}

	<p>You can also write your own loader to fetch templates from a database or key-value store. See <a href="/docs/api/loaders/">Loaders</a>.</p>
{% endblock %}
